K. Hovnanian® Homes is holding an open house Saturday, September 24 and Sunday, September 25 from 11 a.m. to 6 p.m. at 6076 Sauganash Avenue in Chicago.
Available for consumers and brokers to tour will be the Paine Quick Move-In Home. It is located within K. Hovnanian® Homes' Sauganash Glen community, an enclave of 35 brand-new, single-family homes on 4-1/2 acres at 4300 W. Peterson Avenue.
The Paine is one of six floor plans offered at Sauganash Glen. This sophisticated three-story design offers urban appeal with 3,852 square feet of living space, five bedrooms, 3-1/2 baths, and a two-car garage.
On the first floor is the gourmet kitchen, featuring top-of-the-line Wolf™ stainless steel appliances and a Sub Zero® refrigerator along with stylish granite countertops, an arched center island, a ceramic tile backsplash, and 42-inch upper wall cabinets with decorative crown moulding. A formal dining room, intimate study and expansive great room are also on this floor, which is accented by hardwood flooring. Towering 10-foot ceilings and an abundance of windows combine to allow in natural light and create a bright, well-lit interior.
An elegant hardwood staircase leads to the second floor, where the owner's suite is a secluded retreat with a private bath and walk-in closet. Also upstairs are three additional bedrooms and a full bath with ceramic tile, a double-bowl vanity and granite countertop. The second-floor laundry room is an added convenience.
The full finished basement with nine-foot ceilings provides the perfect place for casual everyday living thanks to a family room plus separate entertainment area that is ideal for a gaming station, child's play room or home theater. A guest bedroom is also downstairs for large families or overnight guests.
The exterior of the Paine, as well as all homes at Sauganash Glen, reflects the historic architectural styling of the area. This maintains the established and desired character of the Chicago neighborhood and enhances property values. Marking the entrance to the community is an impressive monument, which is now complete. Additionally, K. Hovnanian® Homes is putting the finishing touches on the property's landscaping to add to the ambiance.
In addition to the Paine Quick Move-In Home on homesite 24-which is priced at $799,995 and is ready to move into now-several homes at Sauganash Glen are under construction, allowing buyers to move in quickly this fall. And for those who prefer to build from the ground up, homes are available that can be tailored to each buyer's specific design selections. Base pricing starts from $799,995. (All homes are available for immediate sale and therefore price and availability are subject to change.)
Designs feature countless modern architectural elements that today's urban buyers are looking for. They range from 3,852 to 4,342 square feet and include a high level of finishes such as quartz countertops in the kitchen and bath, site-finished hardwood flooring on the first and second floor, Smart Home technology with keyless entry, and Nest learning thermostats. In addition, a three-car garage comes with the majority of homesites as space allows.
Visitors can see K. Hovnanian's® quality construction up close by touring the Longfellow decorated model. It is open from 11 a.m. to 6 p.m. daily. The professionally decorated model and sales center is located at 6068 Sauganash Avenue at the corner of Peterson Avenue and Sauganash Avenue in Chicago.
Sauganash Glen is minutes from I-94, making it ideal for professionals commuting to work in the Loop or northern suburbs. The community's proximity to downtown also makes it popular with those who appreciate all the entertainment and restaurants the city offers. For families, the highly acclaimed Sauganash Elementary School, which educates children from kindergarten through eighth grade, is just blocks away. Plus, Sauganash Park and Trail are adjacent to the property. The one-mile trail runs from Bryn Mawr Avenue to Devon Avenue and offers walking and bicycling opportunities for residents.
For more information on Sauganash Glen or this weekend's open house, call (331) 701-7842 or visit www.khov.com/sauganashglen.
