By Francesco Canepa
FRANKFURT, Feb 28 (Reuters) - The European Central Bank said it will test euro zone banks on their resilience to sharp changes in interest rates, simulating scenarios from sudden monetary tightening to the lending freeze that followed Lehman Brothers�� collapse.
The ultra-low or negative ECB rates in place since the start of the financial crisis have eaten into banks�� margins and led them to take on more risk for smaller returns, raising concerns about how the sector might cope once policy is tightened.
